GOAL J14: ENABLE CSR instructions + synchronous traps, get the lockstep clean. Scope = the M1's SUPPORTED Zicsr CSRs + M-mode trap path. EXPLICITLY keep async INTERRUPTS OFF for now (timing injection won't match Spike — separate later wave).

KEY CSR-lockstep rules (do these right, do NOT fake):
1. TIMING CSRs are fundamentally DUT!=Spike (mcycle/mcycleh, minstret/minstreth, time/cycle): the DUT counts real wait/stall cycles, Spike does not. So a `csrr` of a timing CSR legitimately differs. Handle by EXCLUDING timing-CSR read results from the wdata comparison (mark them as do-not-compare), NOT by faking equality. Document which CSRs are excluded and WHY. Non-timing CSR reads/writes (mstatus/mie/mtvec/mepc/mcause/mscratch/mip etc.) MUST still be compared exactly.
2. Constrain riscv-dv to only generate accesses to CSRs the M1 actually implements (no unsupported CSRs unless both DUT and Spike trap identically). Synchronous traps (illegal instr, ecall, ebreak) + mret should be enabled and lockstepped (mepc/mcause/mtval + resume).
3. mtval / mepc / mcause on traps must match (modulo the known base-address normalization already in the comparator).

DO:
1. Edit riscv-dv gen config: enable CSR instr (remove --no_csr_instr) constrained to supported CSRs; enable ebreak/illegal-trap streams; keep interrupts OFF. Configure Spike + DUT identically for trap behavior.
2. Run several seeds. For EACH divergence: root-cause + classify (real-DUT bug -> clean-room fix + ADR; harness/timing-CSR -> correct handling that does NOT mask real DUT bugs). Iterate until clean.
3. RE-VALIDATE after each fix: pytest >=180, gate_03_08 lockstep, gate_02_01 mem_wrapper, gate_04_08 coverage 100%, and prior arith + RV32IMC-noCSR paths still clean.
4. Do NOT launch full 100k yet. Goal = full RV32IMC_Zicsr (CSR + sync traps, no async IRQ) seeds clean.

CONSTRAINTS: clean-room RTL + ADR each; comparator changes must EXCLUDE-not-FAKE timing CSRs and must not mask real DUT bugs; explicit paths.

