codex
There are two real findings from the active CSR sweep. First, this is a REAL-DUT CSR bug: `mstatus` reads `0x00000080` while Spike reads `0x00001880`, because the DUT drops MPP bits. Second is harness configuration: Spike was launched without `zicntr`, so it traps on `cycle`; that is not a DUT bug. I’m fixing both explicitly.
