codex
The next divergence is a REAL-DUT CSR RAW hazard: `csrrw mscratch` retires, but the immediately following `csrr mscratch` reads old data in the DUT while Spike reads the just-written value. I’m fixing this in RTL with CSR write/read forwarding, not by spacing the test or masking the compare.
apply patch
